	(text "C64 USB-C PD Power Adapter v0.2 (DC only, no 50/60 Hz: the C64 TOD clock will not tick from mains)\nNeeds a USB-C PD charger offering 15 V (>= 3 A / 45 W recommended). U1 (CH224A) requests 15 V via R1 = 56k.\nQ1 connects the 15 V rail only after the PD contract (PG low). U2 and U3 start only above ~13.2 V (EN UVLO),\nso a plain 5 V charger, or one that falls back to 9/12 V, never powers the C64.\nDIN: 4+5 = +5.08 V (U2, F1 2 A PTC, D1 TVS), 6 = +12.3 V DC (U3, F2 1.1 A PTC, D2 TVS) into the C64 \"9 VAC\" bridge, 1/2/3/7 = GND.\n12 V DC = the peak of the stock 9 VAC, so user port pins 10/11 see no more than an original PSU gives (but DC, not AC)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
